\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Good Thou art, and good Thou dost,
\par Thy mercies reach to all,
\par Chiefly those who on Thee trust,
\par And for Thy mercy call;
\par New they every morning are;
\par As fathers when their children cry,
\par Us Thou dost in pity spare,
\par And all our wants supply.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Mercy o'er Thy works presides;
\par Thy providence displayed
\par Still preserves, and still provides
\par For all Thy hands have made;
\par Keeps with most distinguished care
\par The man who on Thy love depends;
\par Watches every numbered hair,
\par And all his steps attends.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Who can sound the depths unknown
\par Of Thy redeeming grace;
\par Grace that gave Thine only Son
\par To save a ruined race?
\par Millions of transgressors poor
\par Thou hast for Jesu's sake forgiven,
\par Made them of Thy favour sure,
\par And snatched from hell to heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Millions more Thou ready art
\par To save, and to forgive;
\par Every soul and every heart
\par Of man Thou wouldst receive:
\par Father, now accept of mine,
\par Which now, through Christ, I offer Thee;
\par Tell me now, in love divine,
\par That Thou hast pardoned me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

